WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:04.020
Serial killers, gorgon anatomy, and one very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:08.880
animated disembodied hand. Tim Burton's&nbsp;
"Wednesday" is the perfect family show!

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.060
"Attempted murder. How would&nbsp;
that have looked on your record?"

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:14.868
"Terrible. Everyone would know&nbsp;
I failed to get the job done."

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:20.640
Netflix gave "Wednesday" an eight-episode&nbsp;
season order back in February of 2021,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:25.320
officially getting the ball rolling on the&nbsp;
project. Tim Burton signed on to direct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.480
and executive produce while Al Gough and&nbsp;
Miles Millar also serve as co-showrunners.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:35.940
Production ran from September 2021 to March&nbsp;
2022, so when can we expect to see it?

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:40.320
On September 23, Netflix announced&nbsp;
the series would drop November 23rd&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:46.020
and revealed a brand-new poster. Wednesday&nbsp;
stands poised, twirling an umbrella, outside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:51.540
what is likely Nevermore Academy towering in the&nbsp;
background. As show star Jenna Ortega has stated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:56.640
her version of Wednesday Addams has something&nbsp;
hidden away just below the surface. While the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:01.620
series will miss the Halloween season, "Wednesday"&nbsp;
does arrive just in time for Thanksgiving and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:05.880
quality time with the family. Nothing like good&nbsp;
ole fashioned murder to bring folks together.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:12.120
Netflix's "Wednesday" boasts quite the stacked&nbsp;
cast from top to bottom. As far as the Addams&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:16.800
themselves go, Jenna Ortega plays Wednesday,&nbsp;
Catherine Zeta-Jones portrays her mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:22.320
Morticia, and Luis Guzmán joins them as&nbsp;
family patriarch Gomez. Isaac Ordonez&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:26.580
takes on Wednesday's brother, Pugsley,&nbsp;
George Burcea plays Lurch the butler,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:31.080
and Victor Dorobantu — or his hand, at&nbsp;
least — will appear as Thing. Outside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:35.520
of the Addams family unit, viewers will&nbsp;
get to see a host of incredible actors.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:40.560
The extended cast of "Wednesday" includes&nbsp;
Gwendoline Christie as Larissa Weems,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:47.280
Jamie McShane as Sheriff Donovan Galpin, Joy&nbsp;
Sunday as Bianca Barclay, Emma Myers as Enid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:52.740
Sinclair, Naomi J. Ogawa as Yoko Tanaka,&nbsp;
and a laundry list of other strong names.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:59.220
Additionally, the actress behind the 1990s version&nbsp;
of Wednesday Addams, Christina Ricci, will appear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:03.840
on the Netflix series, though it's unknown who&nbsp;
she'll play. When it comes to Uncle Fester, he is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:08.700
a part of the series, but the character's casting&nbsp;
was at least initially being kept under wraps.

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:14.460
The series is meant to be an offshoot of "The&nbsp;
Addams Family." Netflix describes it as a:

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:18.120
"Sleuthing, supernaturally&nbsp;
infused mystery that follows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:20.040
Wednesday as a student at Nevermore Academy."

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:24.840
"Variety" says that the story will involve&nbsp;
Wednesday developing psychic powers and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:29.700
attempting to control them. In the meantime,&nbsp;
the town surrounding the school is terrorized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:34.200
by an ongoing killing spree. This mystery&nbsp;
appears to involve events from the past,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.900
and apparently has a connection to her parents.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:41.580
Wednesday has to navigate all this while&nbsp;
navigating student life, complete with new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:46.560
relationships and the idiosyncrasies of her fellow&nbsp;
students. We have a feeling she's going to have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:51.060
harder time whipping her new classmates into shape&nbsp;
than those campers at Camp Chippewa in "Addams&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:55.200
Family Values," when she staged a revolt that&nbsp;
eventually led to the destruction of the camp.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:01.560
On August 17, 2022, Netflix gave "Addams&nbsp;
Family" fans what they've been waiting for:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:06.660
the "Wednesday" trailer. Despite clocking in&nbsp;
at just over two minutes long, the teaser did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:10.920
an excellent job of explaining what the series&nbsp;
is all about. We see Wednesday get in trouble&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:15.420
at a school by letting piranhas loose in a&nbsp;
student-occupied pool before we jump to her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:20.040
parents shipping her off to Nevermore Academy.&nbsp;
We get a look at some of the school's personnel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:23.760
students, and the academy itself&nbsp;
as things really go off the rails.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.280
Upon her arrival, we find that Wednesday's new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:29.820
school isn't all that it's cracked up to&nbsp;
be. Wednesday narrates in the trailer:

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:34.800
"Little did I know that I'd be stepping into a&nbsp;
nightmare, full of mystery, mayhem, and murder."

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:39.420
While that might sound horrifying to the average&nbsp;
person, Wednesday has a different feeling.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:41.040
"I think I'm going to love it here."

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:46.680
After a quick and appropriately chaotic montage,&nbsp;
the trailer ends with Wednesday snapping her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:51.240
fingers twice, an incredibly appropriate homage&nbsp;
to the famous "Addams Family" theme song.

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:58.260
Nevermore Academy was founded in 1791. Its sole&nbsp;
mission has been to celebrate and nurture those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:03.060
who lie on the fringes of society. Principal Weems&nbsp;
ponders an interesting question in the trailer.

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:07.140
"In a world full of normies,&nbsp;
do you feel like an outcast?"

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:12.180
She adds that she too has felt like an&nbsp;
oddity and invites the audience to learn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:15.900
more about the academy and all that is in&nbsp;
store through a special video presentation.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:21.600
The Academy offers a wide range of studies,&nbsp;
including Werewolf Reproduction and Gorgon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:25.680
Anatomy. That's only the beginning of the&nbsp;
experience for the students that pass the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:31.320
application process. Extracurricular activities&nbsp;
run the gamut, from painting to archery. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:37.260
academy also boasts such notable alumni as&nbsp;
gothic novelist Edgar Allan Poe and Ignatius It,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:41.580
as well as Morticia and Gomez Addams.&nbsp;
In the words of two of the students,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:46.320
the well-respected institute is open to&nbsp;
"students from all walks of life... and death."

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:52.440
In a featurette released on August 24,&nbsp;
Ortega opens up about her strenuous schedule&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:57.360
preparing to play the show's titular character.&nbsp;
Worried about stepping into the role's legacy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:01.740
she took fencing and cello lessons&nbsp;
twice a week. Her commitment extended&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:06.060
into every facet of the work, including&nbsp;
nailing down Wednesday's physicality.

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:09.240
"I would walk like Wednesday, and&nbsp;
I think that people thought I might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:13.140
be kinda crazy because I wanted her to&nbsp;
be specific and certain and assertive."

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:17.880
Director Tim Burton even compared Ortega's&nbsp;
approach to that of a silent movie actress&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:22.140
because of her ability to convey her thoughts&nbsp;
without words. He praised her performance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:25.920
saying that he couldn't imagine anyone else&nbsp;
in the role. While previous iterations of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:30.360
the character were "cartoony" in Burton's&nbsp;
estimation, a sense of reality was brought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:33.780
to the story to give Wednesday even&nbsp;
more grounded character elements.

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:39.060
Ortega also notes that this Wednesday is much&nbsp;
more socially awkward than previous iterations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:43.320
and her confidence is "more concealed" compared&nbsp;
to what fans may have seen in the past.

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:49.560
Christina Ricci forever immortalized Wednesday&nbsp;
in '90s films "The Addams Family" and "Addams&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:53.280
Family Values." While her role in the&nbsp;
forthcoming series remains top secret,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:56.580
she told Collider that the role&nbsp;
is outrageous and different than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.580 --> 00:06:00.660
anything she'd ever done. She also shared&nbsp;
that she especially enjoyed spending time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:03.780
in a world where everybody seems so&nbsp;
thrilled to be doing the wrong thing.

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:08.220
For Ricci, what makes "Wednesday" even&nbsp;
more special is the fact that Tim Burton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:10.620
asked her directly to be involved. She said,

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:13.860
"To be asked to be part of a new&nbsp;
version of this thing that is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:18.000
huge part of my identity and my history&nbsp;
and my life, I was really touched by it."

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:23.160
While Ricci's Wednesday has a sharp intensity&nbsp;
to it, Ortega's turn brings a different energy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:28.320
one that Ricci thinks is smart, timely and&nbsp;
appropriate. She also observes that the breakout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:33.600
star possesses the, quote, "spirit of dignity&nbsp;
and self-respect that Wednesday's so loved for."

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:39.480
For her part, Ortega commented how "terrified"&nbsp;
she was to be filming with Ricci, especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:45.000
when getting into the exact same costume Ricci&nbsp;
wore 30 years ago. She then swapped compliments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:50.040
noting how Ricci's performance in the '90s films&nbsp;
was "flawlessly done" and "pitch-perfect," adding,

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:54.660
"I wouldn't change anything about it, which is&nbsp;
another reason it was hard for me to do this job."

